  PregFaq(
    id: 'PREG-HEALTH-023',
    number: 133,
    month: 3,
    question: 'What if I choose not to have any screening tests at all? Is that okay?',
    category: 'Health & Medical',
    applicability: 'Month 3 (weeks 9 to 13)',
    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'Yes (light)',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'Yes, choosing not to have NT (nuchal translucency) scan or blood test screening is entirely okay. These tests are voluntary in India, and some women decide the information would not change how they feel about their pregnancy or what they would do, which is a completely valid reason to decline.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.whyMatters, '', [
        'Screening exists to give you information and choice, not to create an obligation. Some women find that the testing process itself, and the waiting for results, causes more anxiety than reassurance, especially if they know they would continue the pregnancy regardless of the result. Recognising this about yourself in advance is a legitimate basis for declining.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'You can decline all optional screening and still receive full, attentive antenatal care; nothing about your routine checkups, scans for your baby\'s growth, or delivery planning depends on having chosen genetic screening. If you change your mind later, some options may still be available depending on your exact stage.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Let your doctor know your preference early so they can adjust your care plan accordingly; you can always ask questions again later if your feelings change.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'There is no single "responsible" choice here; the responsible choice is whatever genuinely fits your own values and peace of mind.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'Screening tests are voluntary, not compulsory.',
        'Declining is a valid choice, especially if results would not change your decisions.',
        'Your routine antenatal care continues fully either way.',
        'Some options may still be available later if you change your mind.',
        'Let your doctor know your preference so care can be adjusted.',
      ]),
    ],
    related: [
      'PREG-SCAN-029',
      'PREG-EMOTION-009',
      'PREG-HEALTH-024',
