  PregFaq(
    id: 'PREG-EMOTION-009',
    number: 134,
    month: 3,
    question: 'How can I manage anxiety while waiting for screening results?',
    category: 'Mental & Emotional Wellbeing',
    applicability: 'Month 3 (weeks 9 to 13)',
    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'Yes',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'Feeling anxious while waiting for scan or blood test results is extremely common and completely understandable. Staying informed about realistic timelines, leaning on your partner or a trusted person, and limiting repeated searching online can all genuinely help this waiting period feel more manageable.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'Waiting for results puts you in a state of uncertainty, and research on couples in this exact situation shows that most people cope by trying to build their own understanding of what is happening, rather than by simply distracting themselves. Some find comfort in talking things through, while others prefer quieter reflection; both are normal responses.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'Ask your doctor upfront how long results usually take, so you know what to expect rather than checking constantly. Try to limit how much time you spend searching symptoms or statistics online, since this often increases worry without adding real information. Sharing how you feel with your partner, a close friend, or family member, rather than carrying it alone, tends to help most people through this period.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'If anxiety is affecting your sleep, appetite, or daily functioning significantly, mention this to your doctor; support is available beyond just the test results themselves.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'Waiting is genuinely one of the harder parts of pregnancy, not because you are doing anything wrong, but because uncertainty is simply difficult to sit with.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'Anxiety while waiting for results is common and understandable.',
        'Ask your doctor for realistic timelines in advance.',
        'Limit repeated online searching, which often increases worry.',
        'Talking to your partner or a trusted person tends to help.',
        'Mention significant anxiety to your doctor; support exists beyond test results.',
      ]),
    ],
    related: [
      'PREG-HEALTH-018',
      'PREG-HEALTH-023',
      'PREG-EMOTION-001',
    ],
  ),
  PregFaq(
    id: 'PREG-HEALTH-024',
    number: 135,
    month: 3,
    question: 'What is genetic counselling, and should I see a genetic counsellor?',
    category: 'Health & Medical',
    applicability: 'Month 3 (weeks 9 to 13)',
    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'Yes (light)',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'A genetic counsellor is a trained specialist who helps you understand your screening or test results, your personal risk factors, and the options available to you, without pushing you toward any particular decision. You do not need a specific reason to ask for a consultation; it is commonly offered after a higher-risk result, due to family history, or simply if you would like more clarity.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.whyMatters, '', [
        'Screening and diagnostic results can involve unfamiliar numbers and terms, and a genetic counsellor\'s role is specifically to translate these into what they mean for your situation, calmly and without judgement. Many Indian hospitals, particularly larger ones, now have dedicated genetic counselling teams working alongside obstetricians for exactly this reason.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'You can ask your doctor for a referral at any point, whether before deciding on a test, after a result you don\'t fully understand, or simply because you want a clearer picture. The conversation covers your options, not a recommendation on what to choose; the decision remains entirely yours.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Ask your doctor whether genetic counselling is available at your hospital, and request it at any stage if it would help.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'Having someone whose only job is to help you understand, without steering you, can make a confusing moment feel a great deal more manageable.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'A genetic counsellor explains results and options without directing your decision.',
        'Commonly offered after a high-risk result, family history, or on request.',
        'Many Indian hospitals have dedicated genetic counselling teams.',
        'You can request this at any stage of your care.',
        'The final decision always remains yours.',
      ]),
    ],
    related: [
      'PREG-HEALTH-018',
      'PREG-SCAN-032',
      'PREG-HEALTH-022',
    ],
  ),
  PregFaq(
