    number: 136,
    month: 3,
    question: 'What does a Down syndrome risk result actually mean for my child?',
    category: 'Health & Medical',
    applicability: 'Month 3 (weeks 9 to 13)',
    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'Yes',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'A Down syndrome risk result from screening only estimates a chance, not a diagnosis; only a test like CVS (chorionic villus sampling) or amniocentesis can confirm it. If your baby does have Down syndrome, it means an extra copy of chromosome 21, which today is associated with a wide, genuinely improving range of health and life outcomes, not a fixed picture.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.whyMatters, '', [
        'Life expectancy and quality of life for people with Down syndrome have improved enormously in recent decades, largely through better cardiac care and early intervention, with average life expectancy now around 60 years compared to far lower figures a few generations ago. Many children benefit significantly from early therapies and inclusive schooling, and most adults with Down syndrome go on to build meaningful, independent lives, including work and close relationships, alongside some ongoing health monitoring, since conditions like heart differences or thyroid issues are somewhat more common and are usually well managed with care.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'If a diagnosis is confirmed, a genetic counsellor or paediatrician can walk you through what it would specifically mean for your family, including local resources and support networks in India. This is a deeply personal moment, and there is no single "right" way to feel or respond.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Ask for a referral to a genetic counsellor and, where relevant, a paediatrician familiar with Down syndrome, to discuss your specific situation in full.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'Whatever you decide or feel in this moment, support and accurate information exist to help you move forward at your own pace, without judgement.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'A risk result is not a diagnosis; only CVS or amniocentesis can confirm it.',
        'Down syndrome means an extra copy of chromosome 21.',
        'Life expectancy and outcomes have improved substantially in recent decades.',
        'Early intervention and good healthcare support meaningful, independent lives.',
        'A genetic counsellor can discuss what this means specifically for your family.',
      ]),
    ],
