    canI: 'Do',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'Under India\'s Maternity Benefit Act, most women working in establishments with 10 or more employees are entitled to 26 weeks of paid maternity leave for their first two children, or 12 weeks for a third child onward. There is no fixed legal deadline for telling your employer, though doing so with reasonable notice, commonly a few months before your expected delivery, gives both of you time to plan.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.whyMatters, '', [
        'The Maternity Benefit Act, amended in 2017, also allows up to 8 weeks of this leave to be taken before your expected delivery date, and gives adopting or commissioning mothers 12 weeks. Larger establishments, those with 50 or more employees, are required to provide creche facilities, and many employers now also permit work-from-home arrangements after leave ends where the role allows it. Exact provisions can differ for government employees, the informal sector, or smaller establishments not covered by the Act.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'Check your specific company\'s policy and your state\'s provisions, since some employers offer more than the legal minimum. Informing HR in writing, with your expected delivery date, helps set your leave dates clearly and protects your entitlements on record.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'This is a workplace and legal matter rather than a medical one; your doctor can confirm your expected delivery date for your employer\'s records if needed.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'Knowing your rights in writing, before you need them, tends to make this conversation with your employer far less stressful when the time comes.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        '26 weeks paid leave for the first two children, 12 weeks for a third.',
        'Applies to establishments with 10 or more employees.',
        'Up to 8 weeks can be taken before your due date.',
        'Adopting and commissioning mothers get 12 weeks.',
        'Confirm your specific company and state provisions with HR.',
      ]),
    ],
    related: [
      'PREG-EMOTION-008',
      'PREG-HEALTH-026',
      'PREG-HEALTH-027',
