        'Several central government schemes offer real financial and healthcare support during pregnancy, most notably the Janani Suraksha Yojana (JSY), which incentivises hospital delivery, and the Pradhan Mantri Matru Vandana Yojana (PMMVY), which gives a cash benefit for a first living child. Many women can register for both, and they are combinable.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.whyMatters, '', [
        'JSY provides a cash incentive for delivering in a government or approved facility, aimed at encouraging safe, institutional births, particularly for women from lower-income households. PMMVY separately provides a cash transfer, commonly cited around five thousand rupees paid in instalments, to support nutrition and healthcare costs during a first pregnancy, tied to attending antenatal checkups and completing early vaccinations. A related scheme, Janani Shishu Suraksha Karyakram (JSSK), aims to make delivery at government facilities entirely free, including free medicines, tests, meals during the hospital stay, and transport.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'Registering early matters, since some benefits are linked to attending antenatal checkups at specific stages. Visit your nearest Anganwadi centre or ask an ASHA worker to help you register for PMMVY and JSY, or check the official PMMVY portal. Eligibility and exact amounts can vary by state.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'This is mainly an administrative matter for your Anganwadi centre or ASHA worker rather than your doctor, though your doctor\'s records may be needed to confirm antenatal visits.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'These schemes exist precisely because pregnancy should not become a financial burden, and registering early means not missing out on support you are entitled to.',
