    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'The NT scan and double marker test only estimate the chance of a small number of specific chromosomal conditions, mainly Down syndrome, Edwards syndrome, and Patau syndrome. They do not detect autism, general intellectual ability, most structural problems, or the vast majority of genetic conditions.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.whyMatters, '', [
        'It is a common and understandable misunderstanding to assume a "normal" first trimester screening result means everything has been checked. In reality, most structural conditions, such as heart, brain, or limb differences, are only reliably seen later, on the detailed anomaly scan around 18 to 22 weeks, since your baby is simply too small now for fine structural detail. Conditions like autism have no prenatal screening test at all, since they are not detected through chromosome analysis or scan measurements.',
