        'If your doctor uses the term "high-risk" at any point, it is always worth asking exactly which meaning they intend, since the two carry very different implications for your care. A high-risk screening result on its own does not automatically make your whole pregnancy high-risk in the broader monitoring sense, and vice versa.',
